Subject: [PATCH 3/3] notmuch: Hide superseded threads from searches
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: nrptukosmntqksqpyqkqokrrynsvwowy
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:15:29 +0000

A superseded tag only cuts the noise if searches leave those threads
out. Excluding the tag by default shows each series once, at its
current version, while a search that names the tag still finds the
old ones for review history.

The package installs the sample only where no config exists, so
existing setups keep their exclusions until they add the tag.
---
change-id: nrptukosmntqksqpyqkqokrrynsvwowy

 dotfiles/notmuch/notmuch-config.sample | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dotfiles/notmuch/notmuch-config.sample b/dotfiles/notmuch/notmuch-config.sample
index 2921e64..069aa92 100644
--- a/dotfiles/notmuch/notmuch-config.sample
+++ b/dotfiles/notmuch/notmuch-config.sample
@@ -21,8 +21,11 @@ primary_email=you@example.com
 [new]
 tags=
 
+# Superseded threads are hidden from searches, so only the current
+# version of each series shows. A query naming the tag still finds
+# them, e.g. tag:superseded.
 [search]
-exclude_tags=deleted
+exclude_tags=deleted;superseded
 
 # Patches carry their commit's jj change id in a Change-Id header, the
 # same across every version of a patch.  changeid:<id> finds them all.
